<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Oceana Fishing lifts yr shr, div.</title>
<headline>Oceana Fishing lifts yr shr, div.</headline>
<dateline>CAPE TOWN 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended Sept 30, 1996</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Headline shr (cts)    48.6	  vs 37.3</p>
<p>    Final div (cts)	 16.6	  making 22.7 vs 19.7</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   52.73	 vs 45.97</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   89.97	 vs 75.58</p>
<p>    Tax			 35.58	 vs 28.67</p>
<p>    Interest paid	    4.77	 vs  2.14</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	4.22	 vs  8.68</p>
<p>    Turnover		  825.66	vs 593.43</p>
<p>Div payable Jan 2</p>
<p>on register Dec 6</p>
<p>Full name: Oceana Fishing Group Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The group said it expected similar or improved levels of total allowable catch for anchovy and pilchard but that the abalone catch had been cut by 10 percent because of environmental factors. The lobster catch had been increased to 1,700 tonnes from 1,500 tonnes.</p>
<p>The lower value of the rand was expected to boost export earnings and the group predicted a &quot;satisfactory&quot; improvement in earnings this year.</p>
<p>The exceptional items were profits on the sale of assets.</p>
<p>-- Cape Town newsroom +27 21 25-2238</p>
</text>
